{"config":{"lang":["en"],"separator":"[\\s\\-]+","pipeline":["stopWordFilter"],"fields":{"title":{"boost":1000.0},"text":{"boost":1.0},"tags":{"boost":1000000.0}}},"docs":[{"location":"index.html","title":"CTF Tool Registry","text":"<p>A personal, CTF-focused knowledge base of tools used in real competitions and writeups.</p> <p>This site exists for one reason:</p> <p>So I never forget what tools exist when solving a challenge.</p>"},{"location":"index.html#categories","title":"Categories","text":"<ul> <li>Web</li> <li>Cryptography</li> <li>Forensics</li> <li>Reverse Engineering</li> <li>Steganography</li> <li>OSINT</li> <li>Miscellaneous</li> <li>Other</li> </ul>"},{"location":"index.html#how-to-use-this-during-a-ctf","title":"How to Use This During a CTF","text":"<ol> <li>Identify the challenge category.</li> <li>Open the corresponding page.</li> <li>Scan the tool list or use site search.</li> <li>Run tools.</li> <li>If a new tool appears in a writeup later \u2014 add it.</li> </ol>"},{"location":"index.html#rules-of-this-registry","title":"Rules of This Registry","text":"<ul> <li>Only tools used in real CTFs or writeups are added.</li> <li>No theory-heavy or enterprise-only tools.</li> <li>This is a tool memory, not a tutorial site.</li> <li>If I forgot a tool once, it belongs here forever.</li> </ul>"},{"location":"index.html#maintenance-workflow","title":"Maintenance Workflow","text":"<ul> <li>During CTF \u2192 use this site</li> <li>After CTF \u2192 read writeups</li> <li>Add missing tools</li> <li>Never rely on memory again</li> </ul>"},{"location":"index.html#status","title":"Status","text":"<p>This registry is intentionally simple.</p> <p>No automation. No overengineering. Just tools that solve flags.</p>"},{"location":"crypto.html","title":"Cryptography Tools \u2013 Complete CTF-Oriented List","text":"<p>This is a strict Markdown, CTF-focused, practical cryptography tools list. Designed for use in a web-based registry (MkDocs / Docusaurus / GitHub Pages).</p>"},{"location":"crypto.html#1-general-first-look-crypto-tools-always-try","title":"1. General / First-Look Crypto Tools (Always Try)","text":"<ul> <li><code>CyberChef</code></li> <li><code>dCode</code></li> <li><code>openssl</code></li> <li><code>python</code></li> <li><code>ipython</code></li> <li><code>bc</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#2-encoding-decoding-tools","title":"2. Encoding / Decoding Tools","text":""},{"location":"crypto.html#common-encodings","title":"Common Encodings","text":"<ul> <li><code>base64</code></li> <li><code>base32</code></li> <li><code>base58</code></li> <li><code>hex</code></li> <li><code>binary</code></li> <li><code>ascii</code></li> <li><code>url encoding</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#obscure-ctf-specific-encodings","title":"Obscure / CTF-Specific Encodings","text":"<ul> <li><code>rot / caesar</code></li> <li><code>atbash</code></li> <li><code>vigenere</code></li> <li><code>rail fence</code></li> <li><code>morse</code></li> <li><code>baconian</code></li> <li><code>playfair</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#3-classical-cipher-tools","title":"3. Classical Cipher Tools","text":"<ul> <li><code>quipqiup</code></li> <li><code>simplesub</code></li> <li><code>pycipher</code></li> <li><code>simplesub-hacker</code></li> <li><code>simplesub-hill</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#4-hash-cracking-analysis","title":"4. Hash Cracking &amp; Analysis","text":"<ul> <li><code>hashcat</code></li> <li><code>john the ripper</code></li> <li><code>hashid</code></li> <li><code>hash-identifier</code></li> <li><code>md5sum</code></li> <li><code>sha1sum</code></li> <li><code>sha256sum</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#5-xor-stream-cipher-tools","title":"5. XOR &amp; Stream Cipher Tools","text":"<ul> <li><code>xor brute scripts</code></li> <li><code>xortool</code></li> <li><code>cribdrag</code></li> <li><code>manytimepad</code></li> <li><code>pwntools</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#6-rsa-asymmetric-crypto-tools","title":"6. RSA / Asymmetric Crypto Tools","text":"<ul> <li><code>RsaCtfTool</code></li> <li><code>rsatool</code></li> <li><code>sageMath</code></li> <li><code>factordb</code></li> <li><code>yafu</code></li> <li><code>msieve</code></li> <li><code>gmpy2</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#7-ecc-advanced-math-crypto","title":"7. ECC / Advanced Math Crypto","text":"<ul> <li><code>sageMath</code></li> <li><code>pari/gp</code></li> <li><code>numpy</code></li> <li><code>sympy</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#8-symmetric-crypto-tools-aes-des-etc","title":"8. Symmetric Crypto Tools (AES, DES, etc.)","text":"<ul> <li><code>openssl enc</code></li> <li><code>pycryptodome</code></li> <li><code>cryptography (python)</code></li> <li><code>aes-bruteforce scripts</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#9-padding-oracle-implementation-attacks","title":"9. Padding / Oracle / Implementation Attacks","text":"<ul> <li><code>padbuster</code></li> <li><code>padding oracle scripts</code></li> <li><code>burp suite</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#10-prng-randomness-attacks","title":"10. PRNG / Randomness Attacks","text":"<ul> <li><code>randcrack</code></li> <li><code>mt19937 predictor</code></li> <li><code>sageMath</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#11-blockchain-web3-crypto-ctf-specific","title":"11. Blockchain / Web3 Crypto (CTF-Specific)","text":"<ul> <li><code>ethers.js</code></li> <li><code>web3.py</code></li> <li><code>foundry</code></li> <li><code>hardhat</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#12-online-crypto-tools-databases","title":"12. Online Crypto Tools &amp; Databases","text":"<ul> <li>CyberChef</li> <li>dCode</li> <li>FactorDB</li> <li>Cryptii</li> </ul>"},{"location":"crypto.html#13-notes","title":"13. Notes","text":"<ul> <li>Crypto CTFs are often layered (encoding \u2192 cipher \u2192 math)</li> <li>Always test weak parameters before brute force</li> <li>Implementation bugs are more common than strong crypto</li> </ul> <p>Rule: If a tool solved a real CTF and is missing \u2014 add it here.</p>"},{"location":"forensics.html","title":"Forensics Tools \u2013 Complete CTF-Oriented List","text":"<p>This is a strict Markdown, CTF-focused, practical digital forensics tools list. Designed for use in a web-based registry (MkDocs / Docusaurus / GitHub Pages).</p>"},{"location":"forensics.html#1-general-first-look-tools-always-use","title":"1. General / First-Look Tools (Always Use)","text":"<ul> <li><code>file</code></li> <li><code>strings</code></li> <li><code>xxd</code></li> <li><code>hexdump</code></li> <li><code>binwalk</code></li> <li><code>binwalk -e</code></li> <li><code>foremost</code></li> <li><code>exiftool</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"forensics.html#2-disk-filesystem-forensics","title":"2. Disk / Filesystem Forensics","text":"<ul> <li><code>Autopsy</code></li> <li><code>The Sleuth Kit (tsk)</code></li> <li><code>fls</code></li> <li><code>icat</code></li> <li><code>mmls</code></li> <li><code>fsstat</code></li> <li><code>mount</code></li> <li><code>losetup</code></li> <li><code>testdisk</code></li> <li><code>photorec</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"forensics.html#3-file-carving-data-recovery","title":"3. File Carving / Data Recovery","text":"<ul> <li><code>foremost</code></li> <li><code>scalpel</code></li> <li><code>photorec</code></li> <li><code>bulk_extractor</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"forensics.html#4-memory-forensics","title":"4. Memory Forensics","text":"<ul> <li><code>Volatility</code></li> <li><code>Volatility3</code></li> <li><code>Rekall</code></li> <li><code>LiME</code></li> <li><code>avml</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"forensics.html#5-network-pcap-forensics","title":"5. Network / PCAP Forensics","text":"<ul> <li><code>Wireshark</code></li> <li><code>tshark</code></li> <li><code>tcpdump</code></li> <li><code>NetworkMiner</code></li> <li><code>Zeek (Bro)</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"forensics.html#6-log-timeline-analysis","title":"6. Log &amp; Timeline Analysis","text":"<ul> <li><code>log2timeline (plaso)</code></li> <li><code>Timesketch</code></li> <li><code>journalctl</code></li> <li><code>last</code></li> <li><code>lastlog</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"forensics.html#7-image-metadata-forensics","title":"7. Image / Metadata Forensics","text":"<ul> <li><code>exiftool</code></li> <li><code>jpeginfo</code></li> <li><code>jhead</code></li> <li><code>pngcheck</code></li> <li><code>tiffinfo</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"forensics.html#8-document-forensics","title":"8. Document Forensics","text":"<ul> <li><code>pdfinfo</code></li> <li><code>pdf-parser</code></li> <li><code>oletools</code></li> <li><code>olevba</code></li> <li><code>officemalscanner</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"forensics.html#9-malware-suspicious-file-analysis","title":"9. Malware / Suspicious File Analysis","text":"<ul> <li><code>strings</code></li> <li><code>pefile</code></li> <li><code>Detect It Easy (DIE)</code></li> <li><code>Capa</code></li> <li><code>YARA</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"forensics.html#10-mobile-forensics-ctf-relevant","title":"10. Mobile Forensics (CTF-Relevant)","text":"<ul> <li><code>adb</code></li> <li><code>sqlite3</code></li> <li><code>androguard</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"forensics.html#11-steg-forensics-hybrid-tools","title":"11. Steg + Forensics Hybrid Tools","text":"<ul> <li><code>binwalk</code></li> <li><code>zsteg</code></li> <li><code>stegsolve</code></li> <li><code>steghide</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"forensics.html#12-online-helper-tools","title":"12. Online / Helper Tools","text":"<ul> <li>VirusTotal</li> <li>CyberChef</li> <li>AnyRun</li> </ul>"},{"location":"forensics.html#13-notes","title":"13. Notes","text":"<ul> <li>Forensics CTFs often combine steg + crypto + filesystem</li> <li>Timestamps and metadata are common hiding places</li> <li>Always check deleted files and slack space</li> </ul> <p>Rule: If a tool appears in a real CTF writeup and is missing \u2014 add it.</p>"},{"location":"misc.html","title":"Miscellaneous Tools \u2013 Complete CTF-Oriented List","text":"<p>This page contains tools that do not fit cleanly into Web, Crypto, Forensics, Reversing, or Steganography but regularly appear in CTF challenges and writeups.</p>"},{"location":"misc.html#1-scripting-automation","title":"1. Scripting &amp; Automation","text":"<ul> <li><code>python</code></li> <li><code>pwntools</code></li> <li><code>bash</code></li> <li><code>perl</code></li> <li><code>node.js</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"misc.html#2-encoding-decoding-transformation","title":"2. Encoding / Decoding / Transformation","text":"<ul> <li><code>CyberChef</code></li> <li><code>dCode</code></li> <li><code>base64</code></li> <li><code>xxd</code></li> <li><code>iconv</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"misc.html#3-file-data-inspection","title":"3. File &amp; Data Inspection","text":"<ul> <li><code>file</code></li> <li><code>strings</code></li> <li><code>hexdump</code></li> <li><code>less</code></li> <li><code>cat</code></li> <li><code>jq</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"misc.html#4-compression-archive-utilities","title":"4. Compression / Archive Utilities","text":"<ul> <li><code>7z</code></li> <li><code>unzip</code></li> <li><code>tar</code></li> <li><code>gzip</code></li> <li><code>bzip2</code></li> <li><code>xz</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"misc.html#5-network-communication-helpers","title":"5. Network &amp; Communication Helpers","text":"<ul> <li><code>netcat (nc)</code></li> <li><code>socat</code></li> <li><code>curl</code></li> <li><code>wget</code></li> <li><code>httpie</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"misc.html#6-diffing-comparison","title":"6. Diffing &amp; Comparison","text":"<ul> <li><code>diff</code></li> <li><code>vimdiff</code></li> <li><code>cmp</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"misc.html#7-regex-text-processing","title":"7. Regex &amp; Text Processing","text":"<ul> <li><code>grep</code></li> <li><code>sed</code></li> <li><code>awk</code></li> <li><code>ripgrep (rg)</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"misc.html#8-time-math-utility-helpers","title":"8. Time, Math &amp; Utility Helpers","text":"<ul> <li><code>bc</code></li> <li><code>date</code></li> <li><code>watch</code></li> <li><code>timeout</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"misc.html#9-container-environment-utilities","title":"9. Container / Environment Utilities","text":"<ul> <li><code>docker</code></li> <li><code>docker-compose</code></li> <li><code>tmux</code></li> <li><code>screen</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"misc.html#10-online-helpers","title":"10. Online Helpers","text":"<ul> <li>CyberChef</li> <li>dCode</li> <li>Regex101</li> <li>GDB Online</li> </ul>"},{"location":"misc.html#notes","title":"Notes","text":"<ul> <li>These tools often bridge multiple categories</li> <li>Many CTF challenges are solved using combinations of tools from this page</li> <li>If a utility solved a real challenge and does not fit elsewhere, it belongs here</li> </ul> <p>Rule: If a tool does not clearly belong to another category but solved a flag, add it here.</p>"},{"location":"osint.html","title":"OSINT Tools \u2013 Complete CTF-Oriented List","text":"<p>This page contains OSINT (Open-Source Intelligence) tools commonly used in CTFs, ARG-style challenges, and investigative tasks.</p> <p>The focus is on practical tools that actually appear in CTF writeups, not enterprise OSINT platforms.</p>"},{"location":"osint.html#1-general-osint-aggregators","title":"1. General OSINT &amp; Aggregators","text":"<ul> <li>OSINT Framework</li> <li>Maltego (Community Edition)</li> <li>SpiderFoot</li> <li>Recon-ng</li> </ul>"},{"location":"osint.html#2-username-identity-enumeration","title":"2. Username / Identity Enumeration","text":"<ul> <li><code>Sherlock</code></li> <li><code>WhatsMyName</code></li> <li><code>Namechk</code></li> <li><code>Namecheckup</code></li> <li><code>Social Analyzer</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"osint.html#3-email-osint","title":"3. Email OSINT","text":"<ul> <li><code>theHarvester</code></li> <li><code>Hunter.io</code></li> <li><code>EmailRep</code></li> <li><code>Have I Been Pwned</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"osint.html#4-domain-website-osint","title":"4. Domain / Website OSINT","text":"<ul> <li><code>WHOIS</code></li> <li><code>dig</code></li> <li><code>nslookup</code></li> <li><code>Amass</code></li> <li><code>Subfinder</code></li> <li><code>crt.sh</code></li> <li><code>SecurityTrails</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"osint.html#5-ip-address-network-osint","title":"5. IP Address &amp; Network OSINT","text":"<ul> <li><code>Shodan</code></li> <li><code>Censys</code></li> <li><code>ZoomEye</code></li> <li><code>IPinfo</code></li> <li><code>AbuseIPDB</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"osint.html#6-image-osint-reverse-image-search","title":"6. Image OSINT (Reverse Image Search)","text":"<ul> <li>Google Reverse Image Search</li> <li>Yandex Images</li> <li>Bing Visual Search</li> <li>TinEye</li> </ul>"},{"location":"osint.html#7-geolocation-maps","title":"7. Geolocation &amp; Maps","text":"<ul> <li>Google Maps</li> <li>Google Earth</li> <li>OpenStreetMap</li> <li>Wikimapia</li> <li>GeoGuessr (logic-based analysis)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"osint.html#8-social-media-osint","title":"8. Social Media OSINT","text":"<ul> <li>Twitter Advanced Search</li> <li>Facebook Graph Search (legacy concepts)</li> <li>Reddit Search</li> <li>Instagram search operators</li> </ul>"},{"location":"osint.html#9-document-metadata-osint","title":"9. Document &amp; Metadata OSINT","text":"<ul> <li><code>exiftool</code></li> <li><code>FOCA</code></li> <li><code>metagoofil</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"osint.html#10-breach-leak-databases","title":"10. Breach &amp; Leak Databases","text":"<ul> <li>Have I Been Pwned</li> <li>DeHashed</li> <li>BreachDirectory</li> </ul>"},{"location":"osint.html#11-dark-web-paste-monitoring-ctf-relevant","title":"11. Dark Web / Paste Monitoring (CTF-Relevant)","text":"<ul> <li><code>Pastebin search</code></li> <li><code>Ghostbin</code></li> <li><code>Search engines with Tor</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"osint.html#notes","title":"Notes","text":"<ul> <li>OSINT CTFs often rely more on thinking and pivoting than tools</li> <li>Google dorking is often more powerful than automation</li> <li>Many flags are hidden in plain sight</li> </ul> <p>Rule: If an OSINT tool helps pivot to the next clue in a real CTF, it belongs here.</p>"},{"location":"other.html","title":"Other Tools \u2013 Complete CTF-Oriented List","text":"<p>This page is a catch-all category for tools, techniques, and utilities that do not clearly belong to Web, Crypto, Forensics, Reversing, Steganography, OSINT, or Miscellaneous, but have appeared in real CTF challenges or writeups.</p> <p>Use this page sparingly. If a tool later fits better in another category, move it.</p>"},{"location":"other.html#1-hardware-physical-side-channel-ctf-relevant","title":"1. Hardware / Physical / Side-Channel (CTF-Relevant)","text":"<ul> <li><code>logic analyzers</code> (Saleae-style)</li> <li><code>ChipWhisperer</code></li> <li><code>Bus Pirate</code></li> <li><code>Arduino / ESP tools</code></li> <li><code>UART / SPI helpers</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"other.html#2-radio-signal-rf","title":"2. Radio / Signal / RF","text":"<ul> <li><code>GNU Radio</code></li> <li><code>GQRX</code></li> <li><code>SDR#</code></li> <li><code>rtl_sdr</code></li> <li><code>URH (Universal Radio Hacker)</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"other.html#3-game-puzzle-logic-challenges","title":"3. Game / Puzzle / Logic Challenges","text":"<ul> <li><code>custom solvers</code></li> <li><code>graph paper / diagrams</code></li> <li><code>constraint solvers</code></li> <li><code>z3</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"other.html#4-ai-ml-image-audio-helpers","title":"4. AI / ML / Image / Audio Helpers","text":"<ul> <li><code>tesseract OCR</code></li> <li><code>OpenCV</code></li> <li><code>pytesseract</code></li> <li><code>speech-to-text tools</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"other.html#5-esoteric-languages-interpreters","title":"5. Esoteric Languages &amp; Interpreters","text":"<ul> <li><code>Brainfuck interpreters</code></li> <li><code>Malbolge interpreters</code></li> <li><code>Whitespace language tools</code></li> <li><code>Piet interpreters</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"other.html#6-build-compilation-runtime-helpers","title":"6. Build / Compilation / Runtime Helpers","text":"<ul> <li><code>gcc</code></li> <li><code>clang</code></li> <li><code>make</code></li> <li><code>cmake</code></li> <li><code>ldd</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"other.html#7-online-external-helpers","title":"7. Online / External Helpers","text":"<ul> <li>Compiler Explorer (Godbolt)</li> <li>WolframAlpha</li> <li>OEIS</li> </ul>"},{"location":"other.html#notes","title":"Notes","text":"<ul> <li>This page exists to avoid forcing tools into the wrong category</li> <li>If multiple tools from here start appearing together, consider creating a new category</li> <li>Minimalism is intentional</li> </ul> <p>Rule: If a tool solved a real CTF challenge and fits nowhere else, add it here.</p>"},{"location":"reversing.html","title":"Reverse Engineering Tools \u2013 Complete CTF-Oriented List","text":"<p>This page contains reverse engineering tools commonly used in CTF challenges and writeups.</p> <p>The focus is on binary analysis, decompilation, debugging, and patching tools that realistically appear in competitions.</p>"},{"location":"reversing.html#1-general-first-look-tools-always-use","title":"1. General / First-Look Tools (Always Use)","text":"<ul> <li><code>file</code></li> <li><code>strings</code></li> <li><code>ldd</code></li> <li><code>checksec</code></li> <li><code>readelf</code></li> <li><code>objdump</code></li> <li><code>nm</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"reversing.html#2-static-analysis-disassembly-decompilation","title":"2. Static Analysis (Disassembly &amp; Decompilation)","text":"<ul> <li><code>Ghidra</code></li> <li><code>IDA Free</code></li> <li><code>Radare2</code></li> <li><code>Cutter</code></li> <li><code>Binary Ninja</code> (Community)</li> <li><code>Hopper</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"reversing.html#3-dynamic-analysis-debugging","title":"3. Dynamic Analysis / Debugging","text":"<ul> <li><code>gdb</code></li> <li><code>pwndbg</code></li> <li><code>gef</code></li> <li><code>lldb</code></li> <li><code>strace</code></li> <li><code>ltrace</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"reversing.html#4-patching-binary-modification","title":"4. Patching &amp; Binary Modification","text":"<ul> <li><code>radare2</code> (patch mode)</li> <li><code>hexedit</code></li> <li><code>Bless</code></li> <li><code>HT Editor</code></li> <li><code>patchelf</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"reversing.html#5-packing-obfuscation-detection","title":"5. Packing / Obfuscation Detection","text":"<ul> <li><code>Detect It Easy (DIE)</code></li> <li><code>PEiD</code></li> <li><code>Exeinfo PE</code></li> <li><code>upx</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"reversing.html#6-scripting-automation","title":"6. Scripting &amp; Automation","text":"<ul> <li><code>pwntools</code></li> <li><code>python</code></li> <li><code>angr</code></li> <li><code>z3</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"reversing.html#7-windows-specific-reverse-engineering","title":"7. Windows-Specific Reverse Engineering","text":"<ul> <li><code>x64dbg</code></li> <li><code>OllyDbg</code></li> <li><code>PE-bear</code></li> <li><code>Resource Hacker</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"reversing.html#8-android-mobile-reverse-engineering","title":"8. Android / Mobile Reverse Engineering","text":"<ul> <li><code>apktool</code></li> <li><code>jadx</code></li> <li><code>dex2jar</code></li> <li><code>smali / baksmali</code></li> <li><code>androguard</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"reversing.html#9-firmware-embedded-reverse-engineering","title":"9. Firmware / Embedded Reverse Engineering","text":"<ul> <li><code>binwalk</code></li> <li><code>Firmware Mod Kit</code></li> <li><code>QEMU</code></li> <li><code>Ghidra</code> (firmware loaders)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"reversing.html#10-online-helper-tools","title":"10. Online / Helper Tools","text":"<ul> <li>Compiler Explorer (Godbolt)</li> <li>Dogbolt</li> <li>GDB Online</li> </ul>"},{"location":"reversing.html#notes","title":"Notes","text":"<ul> <li>Most reversing CTFs are solved using static analysis + light debugging</li> <li>Anti-debug and packing are usually simple in CTFs</li> <li>Scripting (pwntools / python) speeds up repetitive analysis</li> </ul> <p>Rule: If a reversing tool appears in a real CTF writeup and is missing \u2014 add it here.</p>"},{"location":"steganography.html","title":"Steganography Tools \u2013 Complete CTF-Oriented List","text":"<p>This is a strict Markdown list you can directly use in your web-based registry (MkDocs / Docusaurus / GitHub Pages).</p>"},{"location":"steganography.html#1-general-first-look-tools-always-use","title":"1. General / First-Look Tools (Always Use)","text":"<ul> <li><code>file</code></li> <li><code>strings</code></li> <li><code>xxd</code></li> <li><code>hexdump</code></li> <li><code>binwalk</code></li> <li><code>binwalk -e</code></li> <li><code>foremost</code></li> <li><code>exiftool</code></li> <li><code>pngcheck</code></li> <li><code>pdfinfo</code></li> <li><code>identify</code> (ImageMagick)</li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#2-image-steganography-tools","title":"2. Image Steganography Tools","text":""},{"location":"steganography.html#lsb-bit-plane-pixel-analysis","title":"LSB / Bit-Plane / Pixel Analysis","text":"<ul> <li><code>zsteg</code> (PNG, BMP)</li> <li><code>stegsolve</code></li> <li><code>StegOnline</code></li> <li><code>SilentEye</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#image-metadata-structure","title":"Image Metadata &amp; Structure","text":"<ul> <li><code>exiftool</code></li> <li><code>pngcheck</code></li> <li><code>jpeginfo</code></li> <li><code>jhead</code></li> <li><code>tiffinfo</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#visual-channel-based-analysis","title":"Visual &amp; Channel-Based Analysis","text":"<ul> <li><code>ImageMagick</code> (<code>convert</code>, <code>identify</code>)</li> <li><code>GIMP</code></li> <li><code>Photoshop</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#3-password-based-steganography","title":"3. Password-Based Steganography","text":"<ul> <li><code>steghide</code></li> <li><code>OpenStego</code></li> <li><code>SilentEye</code></li> <li><code>OutGuess</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#4-audio-steganography","title":"4. Audio Steganography","text":"<ul> <li><code>Audacity</code></li> <li><code>sox</code></li> <li><code>wavsteg</code></li> <li><code>steghide</code> (audio modes)</li> <li><code>DeepSound</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#5-video-steganography","title":"5. Video Steganography","text":"<ul> <li><code>ffmpeg</code></li> <li><code>SteganoVideo</code></li> <li><code>OpenStego</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#6-text-steganography","title":"6. Text Steganography","text":"<ul> <li><code>SNOW</code></li> <li><code>StegCloak</code></li> <li><code>Whitespace steganography</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#7-compression-embedded-data-detection","title":"7. Compression / Embedded Data Detection","text":"<ul> <li><code>binwalk</code></li> <li><code>7z</code></li> <li><code>unzip</code></li> <li><code>tar</code></li> <li><code>gzip</code></li> <li><code>bzip2</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#8-encoding-multi-layer-steg-helpers","title":"8. Encoding &amp; Multi-Layer Steg Helpers","text":"<ul> <li><code>CyberChef</code></li> <li><code>base64</code></li> <li><code>xxd</code></li> <li><code>xor scripts</code></li> <li><code>rot / caesar</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#9-online-steganography-tools","title":"9. Online Steganography Tools","text":"<ul> <li>StegOnline</li> <li>Aperi'Solve</li> <li>dCode Steganography</li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#10-rare-advanced-ctf-specific-tools","title":"10. Rare / Advanced / CTF-Specific Tools","text":"<ul> <li><code>stegcracker</code></li> <li><code>stego-toolkit</code></li> <li><code>zlib-flate</code></li> <li><code>bmpsteg</code></li> <li><code>PngSuite</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#11-manual-human-based-analysis-do-not-skip","title":"11. Manual / Human-Based Analysis (Do Not Skip)","text":"<ul> <li>Zoom &amp; inspect pixels</li> <li>Adjust brightness / contrast</li> <li>Flip / rotate image</li> <li>Change color spaces</li> </ul>"},{"location":"steganography.html#12-notes","title":"12. Notes","text":"<ul> <li>No single tool finds everything</li> <li>Always assume multi-layer steganography</li> <li>Many CTFs combine steg + crypto + encoding</li> </ul> <p>Last rule: If a tool was used in a writeup and is missing here \u2014 add it. Thanks for reading.</p>"},{"location":"web.html","title":"Web Tools \u2013 Complete CTF-Oriented List","text":"<p>This page contains web exploitation tools commonly used in CTF challenges and writeups.</p> <p>The focus is on CTF-style web problems (logic bugs, auth bypass, source leaks, injections), not full enterprise pentesting stacks.</p>"},{"location":"web.html#1-general-first-look-tools-always-use","title":"1. General / First-Look Tools (Always Use)","text":"<ul> <li><code>Browser DevTools</code></li> <li><code>view-source</code></li> <li><code>curl</code></li> <li><code>wget</code></li> <li><code>httpie</code></li> <li><code>Burp Suite (Community)</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#2-interception-request-manipulation","title":"2. Interception &amp; Request Manipulation","text":"<ul> <li><code>Burp Suite</code> (Proxy, Repeater)</li> <li><code>OWASP ZAP</code></li> <li><code>mitmproxy</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#3-directory-file-enumeration","title":"3. Directory &amp; File Enumeration","text":"<ul> <li><code>ffuf</code></li> <li><code>gobuster</code></li> <li><code>dirsearch</code></li> <li><code>feroxbuster</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#4-parameter-discovery-fuzzing","title":"4. Parameter Discovery &amp; Fuzzing","text":"<ul> <li><code>ffuf</code> (params mode)</li> <li><code>arjun</code></li> <li><code>paramspider</code></li> <li><code>wfuzz</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#5-authentication-logic-bugs","title":"5. Authentication &amp; Logic Bugs","text":"<ul> <li><code>Burp Repeater</code></li> <li><code>Turbo Intruder</code></li> <li><code>custom scripts</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#6-sql-injection","title":"6. SQL Injection","text":"<ul> <li><code>sqlmap</code></li> <li><code>Burp Suite</code></li> <li><code>manual payloads</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#7-xss-client-side-testing","title":"7. XSS / Client-Side Testing","text":"<ul> <li><code>XSStrike</code></li> <li><code>dalfox</code></li> <li><code>Burp DOM Invader</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#8-ssti-template-injection","title":"8. SSTI / Template Injection","text":"<ul> <li><code>tplmap</code></li> <li><code>SSTI payloads</code></li> <li><code>Burp Suite</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#9-file-upload-deserialization","title":"9. File Upload &amp; Deserialization","text":"<ul> <li><code>Burp Suite</code></li> <li><code>ysoserial</code></li> <li><code>phpggc</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#10-jwt-session-attacks","title":"10. JWT / Session Attacks","text":"<ul> <li><code>jwt_tool</code></li> <li><code>jwt.io debugger</code></li> <li><code>Burp Suite</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#11-web-crypto-encoding-helpers","title":"11. Web Crypto / Encoding Helpers","text":"<ul> <li><code>CyberChef</code></li> <li><code>hashcat</code></li> <li><code>openssl</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#12-source-code-secret-discovery","title":"12. Source Code &amp; Secret Discovery","text":"<ul> <li><code>ripgrep</code></li> <li><code>git</code></li> <li><code>git-dumper</code></li> <li><code>trufflehog</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#13-websockets-apis","title":"13. WebSockets &amp; APIs","text":"<ul> <li><code>Burp WebSockets</code></li> <li><code>websocat</code></li> <li><code>Postman</code></li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#14-online-helpers","title":"14. Online Helpers","text":"<ul> <li>CyberChef</li> <li>RequestBin / Webhook.site</li> <li>Regex101</li> </ul>"},{"location":"web.html#notes","title":"Notes","text":"<ul> <li>Web CTFs often hide flags in logic, not vulnerabilities</li> <li>Manual testing beats automation in most challenges</li> <li>Always inspect JavaScript and API responses</li> </ul> <p>Rule: If a web tool solves a real CTF challenge and is missing \u2014 add it here.</p>"}]}